          "title": "B-tree Index Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Tree and leaves",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Sorted, balanced tree== of key values pointing to rows",
                "Point lookup: ==O(log n)==",
                "Range scan or `ORDER BY` on the key: ==O(log n + k)== for the k rows read"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Root",
                    "sub": "entry point",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Internal nodes",
                    "sub": "route by key",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Leaf pages",
                    "sub": "linked in key order",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Range scan finds the start **once**, then walks the linked leaves"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Seek vs scan",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Index seek",
                "Full table scan"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Does",
                  "Jumps to a key",
                  "Reads every row"
                ],
                [
                  "Reads",
                  "Few",
                  "All"
                ],
                [
                  "Wins when",
                  "Small fraction of rows",
                  "Most rows needed"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`WHERE customer_id = 42` seeks the tree once the column is indexed"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX idx_orders_cust ON orders(customer_id);",
                "SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 42;"
              ],
              "note": "seeks the tree instead of scanning the table"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Indexing every column: each index costs ==disk space==",
                "Every index slows `INSERT`, `UPDATE` and `DELETE`",
                "Low-selectivity columns (gender, boolean) rarely help"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Composite and Covering Indexes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Composite and Covering Indexes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Order and the Leftmost Prefix",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Index on `(a, b, c)` is sorted by ==a==, then **b** within a, then **c** within b",
                "Usable from the left only: the ==leftmost prefix=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Filter on",
                "Serves it?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`a`",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`a, b`",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`a, b, c`",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`b` alone",
                  "{red:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "`c` alone",
                  "{red:no}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Column Order",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Equality} columns first, ==range== column last",
                "Break ties by **higher selectivity**",
                "Columns after a range condition ==cannot narrow== the seek"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX idx_orders_cust_status_date",
                "ON orders(customer_id, status, created_at);"
              ],
              "note": "two equalities, then the range column"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Covering Indexes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Covering==: every column the query needs is in the index",
                "Plan shows `Index Only Scan` or `Using index`: no table lookup",
                "Extra columns: `INCLUDE` (Postgres, SQL Server) or trailing key columns (MySQL)"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX idx_cov ON orders(customer_id) INCLUDE (total);",
                "CREATE INDEX idx_cov ON orders(customer_id, total);"
              ],
              "note": "first: Postgres, SQL Server; second: MySQL"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Redundant index",
              "text": "Creating both `(a)` and `(a, b)` is a mistake: the composite already serves queries on a, so `(a)` is ==redundant==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "When Indexes Are Not Used",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "When Indexes Are Not Used",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Predicate hides the column",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Function} on the column hides the sorted key",
                "{red:Leading %}: `LIKE 'abc%'` is a ==prefix range==; `'%abc'` is not",
                "{red:Type mismatch}: VARCHAR vs number ==casts every row=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Skipped",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`YEAR(created_at) = 2025`",
                  "range on bare column"
                ],
                [
                  "`LOWER(email) = 'a@b.com'`",
                  "functional index"
                ],
                [
                  "`LIKE '%abc'`",
                  "`LIKE 'abc%'` or full-text"
                ],
                [
                  "`phone = 5551234`",
                  "`phone = '5551234'`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "WHERE created_at >= '2025-01-01'",
                "  AND created_at <  '2026-01-01'",
                "CREATE INDEX idx_email_lower",
                "  ON users (LOWER(email));"
              ],
              "note": "rewrite the predicate, or index the expression"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Scan is cheaper",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Query returns ==~10-20%+== of rows: {orange:full scan} wins",
                "Random lookups cost more than one sequential read",
                "{orange:Tiny table}: a scan is already cheap",
                "{orange:Stale stats}: run `ANALYZE` / `UPDATE STATISTICS`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. More skips",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`OR` across different columns",
                "`<>` and `NOT IN`",
                "Leftmost prefix violated: `(a,b)` filtered on `b` alone"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Check",
              "text": "Keep the ==bare column== on one side, then confirm with EXPLAIN: Index Scan, not Seq Scan."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "EXPLAIN and Sargable Queries",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
